{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "quarter-ice-perpetual-cycle",
  "title": "Quarter Ice Perpetual Cycle",
  "description": "A quarter-ice drill to work on both the high cycle and the low cycle, a modification of the Perpetual Cycle drill for smaller spaces or groups too large to keep everyone moving in the original. One line of skaters. P1 dumps the puck in to the corner and swings in to pick it up; P2 follows up and receives the cycle; a cycle give and go ends in a shot. P3 dumps the puck in on the other side of the net, P2 loops back into the zone and cycles the other way, and P3 follows up, receives the cycle and passes out front to P2. The drill repeats.",
  "tags": [
    "cycle",
    "passing",
    "shooting",
    "offence"
  ],
